[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1083","stub":{"id":"1083","section":"1. Route 1545 (Chicken Bridge) to US Route 15-501 (Bynum)","altname":"Upper Haw","river":"Haw","difficulty":"ItoIIstandoutIII","states":["USA-NCR"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"169","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"This is the old path to the put in launch, obstructed by no less than 7 trees down, thanks to Chantal July 2025. Now, I would turn right before this mess, to take the path under the bridge towards the swimming hole, which is not without obstacles, but a fairly decent alternative to the old launch. Note that there is not a very good cell signal here at all and the usual route that is taken to set shuttle at the dam (River road to Hamlets Chapel to Moore Mountain to 15-501) is detoured due to multiple road washouts, so plan to drive across the bridge and take Old Graham to Russel Chapel to 15-501 (all lefts) to get to the take out to set shuttle.","id":"110990","location":{"latitude":"35.8324","longitude":"-79.2188"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":"I6qehyE8hj1enV0sYdM32","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"The first major rapid on this section of the Haw. There are rapids on either side of an island. On the left, there is a rocky Class I. On the right, there is a slighty more technical, but fun rapid named, Sawtooth Ledge (II). The rocks at the end of this rapid are sometimes hard to avoid. Photo shows what it looks like from the bottom of the rapid at ~1,200 cfs","id":"2619","location":{"latitude":"35.818084","longitude":"-79.197102"},"name":"Sawtooth Ledge","distance":"1.87","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"pcdUB7UtJTXFleSSmQXcE"},{"type":"playspot","description":"The next rapid really does not have name. It is an ok playspot. It is a nice spot to step out of your boat and stretch.","id":"2645","location":{"latitude":"35.816582","longitude":"-79.185754"},"name":"Lunchstop (Upper Haw)","distance":"2.76","difficulty":"I","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"playspot","description":"This rapid is recognized by old bridge supports. Run this rapid towards the center, in the main flow. Fun rapid to surf.","id":"2646","location":{"latitude":"35.803289","longitude":"-79.182081"},"name":"Little Nantahala","distance":"3.78","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"This is the last rapid before the Bynum Dam slack water. According to guidebooks and CCC mailing lists, canoes love to broach on this rapid.","id":"2647","location":{"latitude":"35.790599","longitude":"-79.1764"},"name":"Final Solution","distance":"4.8","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"takeout","description":"Take-out for the Upper Haw. Portage around the dam on river left. Running this dam, like all dams, is not recommended.","id":"2648","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Bynum Dam","distance":"6.7","photoID":null,"difficulty":null,"approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"pcdUB7UtJTXFleSSmQXcE","ext":"jpg","post_id":"uY36LAoaFJkig3944h8hi","description":"","caption":"The bottom of Sawtooth","poi_name":null,"subject":"This is what it looks like from the bottom of the rapid at ~1,200 cfs","author":"Sonia Dekker","poi_id":"2619","photo_date":"2025-07-16T15:52:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-07-16T15:52:25.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/pcdUB7UtJTXFleSSmQXcE","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/pcdUB7UtJTXFleSSmQXcE"}},{"id":"I6qehyE8hj1enV0sYdM32","ext":"jpg","post_id":"uY36LAoaFJkig3944h8hi","description":"<p>Now, I would turn right to take the path under the bridge towards the swimming hole, which is not without obstacles, but a fairly decent alternative to the old launch.</p>","caption":"Original Put in Post Chantal July 2025","poi_name":null,"subject":"This is the old put-in, I guess Chantal created a new one. ","author":"Sonia Dekker","poi_id":"110990","photo_date":"2025-07-16T15:52:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-07-16T15:52:25.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/I6qehyE8hj1enV0sYdM32","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/I6qehyE8hj1enV0sYdM32"}},{"id":"SDEpJAzQRQigyhCrTT6af","ext":"jpg","post_id":"uY36LAoaFJkig3944h8hi","description":"<p>Bynum Gauge was reading about 1,000 cfs at this time of day</p>","caption":"General area of Final Solution ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Sonia Dekker","poi_id":"2647","photo_date":"2025-07-16T15:52:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-07-16T15:52:26.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/SDEpJAzQRQigyhCrTT6af","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/SDEpJAzQRQigyhCrTT6af"}},{"id":"890060","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892537","description":"","caption":"Upper HAW14,000 cfs 27OCT18 Hala Atcha 9'6","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Ken","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890060","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890060"}},{"id":"890061","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892538","description":"","caption":"Upper HAW14,000 cfs 27OCT18 Hala Atcha 9'6","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Ken","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890061","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890061"}},{"id":"890062","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892539","description":"","caption":"Upper HAW14,000 cfs 27OCT18 Hala Atcha 9'6","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Ken","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890062","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890062"}},{"id":"890063","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892540","description":"","caption":"Upper HAW14,000 cfs 27OCT18 Hala Atcha 9'6","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Ken","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890063","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890063"}},{"id":"890064","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892541","description":"","caption":"Upper HAW14,000 cfs 27OCT18 Hala Atcha 9'6","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Ken","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890064","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890064"}}],"detail":{"id":"1083","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"**Put-in:**\n\nThe put-in for this section is on Chicken Bridge Road on river left. The put-in is about 100 yards down a small trail. The put-in itself is very treacherous and requires near vertical portage.\n\n**Take-out:**\n\nThe take-out is right above the Bynum dam on river left. Parking is available off of US 15-501. This is also the put-in for the Middle Haw.\n\n**Description:**\n\nThe Upper Haw is a nice section of river through rural Chatham County. This section is ideal for beginners, novices, and intermediate paddlers. Most rapids are boat scoutable. From the put-in there are small rapids providing opportunities to test skills. This section of river has many unnamed rapids. The larger rapids include Sawtooth Ledge, Little Nantahala and Final Solution.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"6.8","correlations":[{"reachID":"1083","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDif